Better Files

This mod is derived from the Files mod shipped with Herdr App 0.1.15.
The installed Herdr distribution includes the Apache License, Version 2.0.
A copy is retained in LICENSE.

Original Files main.js SHA-256:
8296131be2d680db91711f1cd3a79d67de6b11b3328c06dfe8957028ec9bf7cf

Changes in this copy:
- main.js captures each row's workspace root, space ID, and machine identity.
- An unrelated space folder is replaced with the browsed folder as the reader root.
- Markdown opens in a retained reader view inside the Files pane.
- Back, Escape, unmodified Backspace, replacement, and parent close clean up the reader before entity release.
- Other previews and directory navigation retain their original routes.
- Icon paths use mods/better-files.
- mod.json names the personal clone, enables focus, and records its source version.
- jsconfig.json uses the repository's runtime-only type-check settings.
- Type annotations and formatting match the installed SDK and repository rules.

markdown.js, tests, native checks, and documentation are additions.
The four copied icons add accessibility titles. Their geometry is unchanged.
Their ISC and MIT notices are retained in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.

reader/ contains the Markdown Reader UI, model, host runtime, Node launcher,
helper, document parser, file/cache handling, and renderers. This reader source
retains its separate MIT license in reader/LICENSE. DEPENDENCIES.md records
runtime dependency licenses and pinned versions; Chromium has its own notices.
No Morsel AGPL source is included.

reader/main.js removes the file/root picker, its input state, and the Open
control. Documents open from captured entry props or validated local links;
failures show an error. Local links replace the session in the same view and
wait for previous cleanup. The standalone reader Open/dialog/tab API and
Files-clone preparation tool are retired; better-files is the only mod root.

reader/runtime.js invokes the local helper at
<app-home>/mods/better-files/reader/helper.mjs. Requests, assets, render metadata,
and leases use <app-home>/data/better-files/. The merged runtime does not read,
migrate, or automatically delete data/markdown-reader/. Source Markdown is not
written. reader/node.js finds installed Node.js 26+ through persistent Windows
PATH or fnm when the app cannot find node on its inherited PATH. It changes no
persistent environment setting. reader/helper.mjs retains import.meta.main for
CLI entry through junctions and symbolic links.

